# Recipe: keep the bundled omi-audio, transcribe with OpenAI's API.
# PRIVACY: every utterance you record is sent to OpenAI and billed per minute.
# See README.md for what this changes and why.
#
# Apply: copy the uncommented lines into omi-host/.env, then
#   cd omi-host && docker compose up -d

OMI_ASR_ENGINE=openai
OMI_ASR_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
OMI_ASR_API_KEY=sk-REPLACE-ME

# whisper-1 returns per-segment timestamps.
OMI_ASR_MODEL=whisper-1

# gpt-4o-transcribe / gpt-4o-mini-transcribe are more accurate but only answer
# "json" (text, no segments): each utterance becomes one segment. omi-audio
# would discover that on its first request; setting it skips the failed try.
# OMI_ASR_MODEL=gpt-4o-transcribe
# OMI_ASR_RESPONSE_FORMAT=json

# Optional: OpenAI voices for spoken replies instead of the local Piper voice.
# OMI_TTS_ENGINE=openai
# OMI_TTS_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OMI_TTS_API_KEY=sk-REPLACE-ME
# OMI_TTS_MODEL=tts-1
# OMI_TTS_VOICE=alloy

# Nothing transcribes on the GPU any more; run diarization on the CPU too and
# omi-audio holds no VRAM at all.
# OMI_DIA_DEVICE=cpu
